1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,390
Somewhere, a clanmate just got a Twisted bow.

2
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:06,710
They're looking for the screenshot key.

3
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:09,170
Your Discord will hear about it in forty minutes.

4
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:10,230
Or never.

5
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:13,860
Or it could hear about it in seconds.

6
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:23,300
The DropTracker is a RuneLite plugin and a Discord bot,

7
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:24,460
working as a pair.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,200
Your members just play.

9
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:32,600
The plugin spots the loot, the personal bests, the collection log slots and the pets,

10
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,220
takes the screenshot itself, and sends it in.

11
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:39,390
A moment later it's in your Discord.

12
00:00:40,690 --> 00:00:45,050
The item, what it's worth, the kill count, the screenshot,

13
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:47,890
and where they now rank in your clan this month.

14
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:50,050
Nobody typed a thing.

15
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,140
You decide what that message looks like.

16
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:58,800
Every part of the design is yours to change, and it's free.

17
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:01,990
And you decide what deserves one.

18
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:06,190
Drops under two and a half million stay quiet by default,

19
00:01:06,190 --> 00:01:08,370
so nobody's announcing rune scimitars.

20
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:14,050
Personal bests, pets and collection logs can each get their own channel.

21
00:01:15,030 --> 00:01:17,650
Deaths are available too, if your clan enjoys that.

22
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:22,720
Meanwhile the lootboard keeps score: a picture of this month's loot,

23
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:25,440
redrawn on its own and edited in place.

24
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:30,560
And your clan gets its own pages on droptracker.

25
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:31,920
io.

26
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,820
Useful for settling arguments.

27
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:36,620
Or starting them.

28
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:41,940
Membership follows your Wise Old Man group and syncs every hour.

29
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,240
New recruits show up.

30
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,780
People who left, leave.

31
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:48,640
And because someone will always try it:

32
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,540
big drops are checked against the OSRS Wiki's drop tables.

33
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:57,620
A Twisted bow from a goblin doesn't get recorded, let alone announced.

34
00:01:58,630 --> 00:02:03,910
When you want more, run bingos that score themselves, keep a clan points ledger,

35
00:02:03,910 --> 00:02:07,490
or post a Hall of Fame of your fastest kills.

36
00:02:08,790 --> 00:02:11,330
Points and the Hall of Fame are on paid plans.

37
00:02:12,070 --> 00:02:17,030
The notifications, the lootboard, the designs and your clan's pages are free.

38
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:20,090
Setup takes a few minutes.

39
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:23,850
Pick your Discord server, invite the bot,

40
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:26,530
paste in your Wise Old Man group, and choose a channel.

41
00:02:27,350 --> 00:02:30,270
Then tell your clan to install the DropTracker plugin.

42
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:33,810
Screenshots were never the fun part anyway.
